    {
      "id": "problem_solution",
      "skeleton": "/Users/suryakrishnan/Documents/GitHub/overview_consulting/screenshot_generator/deck/skeletons/_shared/problem_solution.pptx",
      "tokens": {
        "problem": "The part is a long, formed sheet-metal tail rail held in a fixture on the line. Three conditions have to be confirmed on every part: cracks anywhere along the body of the rail, presence of six punched holes along the flange, and the quality of the flared \"horn\" end (missing-end / surface condition). Inspection runs in-line, with the plant PLC triggering the camera on each cycle, so the verdict must be produced automatically and returned to the controls system.",
        "solution": "A single Overview AI camera runs one recipe with three AI models: pixel-level crack segmentation across five zones tiling the rail, a hole-presence classifier on six hole locations, and a horn-quality (missing end) classifier on the end feature. Both classifiers reached 100% training accuracy \u2014 horn quality on 30 labeled examples (23 Pass / 7 Fail) and hole presence on 83 labeled examples (74 pass / 9 fail) \u2014 while the crack model trained down to 0.028 loss. The camera combines all three results into one pass/fail verdict and sends it to the plant PLC over industrial Ethernet on every cycle, with a detailed result report also forwarded to the cell's master controller."
      }
    },
